{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "The comparer's own idea of 'the same effect' (PLAN Phase 6: it must not reuse the converter's field map). Hand-written from n8n's public node docs, the services' REST API docs and the captured connector schemas in evals/mocks/connectors. Each rule maps one side's raw call to a canonical effect {service, action, target, fields}. http rules apply to n8n's outgoing requests (the mock log) and to the runner's http requests alike; tool rules apply to connector calls on the Claude side. Field paths: body.x, query.x, path.<group>, args.x, mime.<Header>|mime.text (a Gmail raw message), multipart.<field> (the JSON part of a multipart upload), reply.thread|recipient|cc|subject (the message a reply tool call answers, by the rule's replyTo id, as the fixture serves it: compare.mjs refsOf/replyFields); a list of paths takes the first that is present. Comparison per field: exact (JSON equal), set (lists, order ignored; a single value counts as a one-item list), id (strings, dashes and case ignored), text (model-written when a model reply is in it; else exact after trimming), subject (leading Re:/Fw:/Fwd: dropped; wins over the other side's rule). A Gmail raw body is decoded by its Content-Transfer-Encoding (base64 or quoted-printable).",
  "sources": [
    "https://developers.google.com/gmail/api/reference/rest/v1/users.messages (list, get, modify, send, trash) and users.drafts.create, users.threads.modify",
    "https://developers.google.com/gmail/api/guides/threads (a reply joins the thread by threadId, References/In-Reply-To and a matching Subject) and RFC 5322 3.6.3 (a reply goes to Reply-To, else From; reply-all adds To and Cc)",
    "https://developers.google.com/drive/api/reference/rest/v3/files (get with alt=media, list, create via /upload with uploadType multipart|resumable, update with addParents/removeParents, copy, delete)",
    "https://developers.google.com/sheets/api/reference/rest/v4/spreadsheets.values/append and spreadsheets.get",
    "https://developers.notion.com/reference (retrieve a database GET /v1/databases/{id}, query POST /v1/databases/{id}/query, create a page POST /v1/pages, update PATCH /v1/pages/{id}, append children PATCH /v1/blocks/{id}/children)",
    "https://api.slack.com/methods/chat.postMessage",
    "https://core.telegram.org/bots/api#sendmessage and #sendphoto",
    "https://developer.wordpress.org/rest-api/reference/posts/ and /media/",
    "https://developers.facebook.com/docs/instagram-platform/content-publishing (POST /{ig-user-id}/media, POST /{ig-user-id}/media_publish, GET /{container-id}?fields=status_code)",
    "https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/images/create and /assistants (threads, runs, messages)",
    "https://replicate.com/docs/reference/http#models.predictions.create",
    "https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/API:Main_page (GET /w/api.php)",
    "https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/builtin/app-nodes/ (Gmail, Google Drive, Google Sheets, Notion, Slack, Telegram, WordPress, Facebook Graph API node operations, 2026-11-14)",
    "evals/mocks/connectors/*.json (captured tool names and input schemas)"
  ],
  "ignore": [
